\begin{proof}
Let $X_t=I_{9t+6}$, and ${\cal G}_t=\{\{i\}:0\leq
i\leq 9t-1\}\cup\{\{9t,9t+1,\dots,9t+5\}\}$. Then $(X_t,{\cal
G}_t,{\cal C}_t)$ is a $[3,1]$-GDC$(6)$ of type $1^{9t}6^1$,
where ${\cal C}_t$ is obtained by developing the codewords in Table~\ref{t1^9t6^1} under the automorphism group
$G_t$.

For $t\in\{2,3\}$, $G_t=\langle(0\ \ 3\ \ 6\ \ \cdots\ \
9t-3)(1\ \ 4\ \ 7\ \ \cdots\ \ 9t-2)(2\ \ 5\ \ 8\ \ \cdots\ \
9t-1)(9t\ \ 9t+1\ \ 9t+2)(9t+3\ \ 9t+4\ \ 9t+5)\rangle$.

For $t\in\{5,7,9\}$, $G_t=\langle(0\ \ 1\ \ 2\ \ \cdots\ \ 9t-1)(9t\
\ 9t+1\ \ 9t+2)(9t+3\ \ 9t+4\ \ 9t+5)\rangle$.
\end{proof}

